      <div>
        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · Islamic Caliphates &amp; Middle East</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Damascus</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 2500 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">First settled in the 3rd millennium BCE; carbon-14 dating at Tell Ramad on its outskirts suggests occupation from about 6300 BCE, but no large-scale settlement lay within the present walls until the second millennium BCE. Greek myths and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josephus">Josephus</a> name founders of their own.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On a plateau 680 metres above sea level, about 80 km inland from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, on the eastern foothills of the Anti-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a> mountains and the Barada River.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Aram-Damascus; the Roman plan of the Old City; capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> from 661 to 750; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-mosque">Umayyad Mosque</a>; the Ayyubid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> periods; the sack by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> in 1401; the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajj">Hajj</a> caravans; capital of the French Mandate and of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Damascus is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, and its Old City is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</span></div>
